title: The Rentenmark
subtitle: The inflation is over, and the works are paying for it.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 12 and e23_rentenmark_done = 0 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('The Rentenmark holds: bread costs the same at night', 3);
Q.e23_rentenmark_done = 1;
Q.inflation = 12;
Q.stability += 12;
if (Q.e22_workers_gov == 0) {
    Q.chancellor = 'Wilhelm Marx';
    Q.government_name = 'Marx cabinet (Centre, DDP, DVP, BVP)';
    Q.spd_in_government = 0; Q.zentrum_in_government = 1; Q.ddp_in_government = 1; Q.dvp_in_government = 1; Q.bvp_in_government = 1;
}
!}

= The Rentenmark

The new Rentenmark went into circulation on 15 November at one to a trillion old marks. Schacht stopped the presses, and the new money holds. By December a loaf costs the same in the evening as it did in the morning. [? if e22_workers_gov = 0 : Stresemann lost a vote of confidence on 23 November, and Wilhelm Marx of the Centre governs without the SPD. ?]

The bill comes to the works. The Reich dismisses officials by the hundred thousand, the employers lengthen the working day by decree, and the eight-hour day of November 1918 is gone in most of the country.

- @hours: Fight for the eight-hour day works by works.
- @unemployed: Organise the unemployed at the labour exchanges.
- @dues: Collect the dues in the new money.

@hours
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Most of these strikes will be lost. The workers will remember who led them.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids work inside the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('union_work');
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Our factory cells lead a hundred small strikes over the length of the shift. Siemens gives way in one plant and sacks the strike committee in another.

@unemployed
subtitle: A new base in Berlin and the Ruhr, among men with nothing to lose.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('berlin', {militancy: 4, members: 0.04});
RG.district('ruhr', {militancy: 4, members: 0.04});
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Committees of the unemployed meet in the queues outside the labour exchanges in Wedding and Gelsenkirchen. The first march on the Berlin town hall is three thousand strong.

@dues
subtitle: For the first time in a year the party's money will be worth something. Some members will not pay.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources += 2;
Q.districts.forEach(function (d) { RG.district(d, {members: -0.04}); });
!}

The district treasurers go round with the cards. Dues are twenty pfennigs a week, in the new money, and the treasurers write down the names of those who will not pay.
